{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791818778,"nonce":"V7veMniT7gsKr9XNHXoSMRjTvHQ=","message":"Decision: A1 spike changes two parts of the 022 design. (1) Orphan removal: chrome.runtime.id is still set inside port.onDisconnect after a reload and clears about 50 ms later, so the handler must defer the id check (about 250 ms); spec text updated. (2) Submit watch: submit.isTrusted is true even for script-made submits (requestSubmit, el.click), userActivation.isActive is true for 5 s after any real click or a browser navigation, and form.submit() fires no event; A9 must key on a trusted click on the submitter (or Enter keydown) before the submit event plus a non-null submitter, never on submit.isTrusted or isActive alone. Reason: measured in Chromium 153 via Playwright, see the A1 spike findings section in specs/022-extension-apply-assist.md and tests/e2e/test_spike_022_a1.py on branch bug/9e2c202-ext-spike. Everything else held: sidePanel.open works synchronously from a relayed click (fails after one await), windows.create fallback works, panel is not a Playwright page so e2e asserts via runtime.getContexts and the panel hello, setAccessLevel hides storage.local from content scripts, 3 MB base64 resume is byte-identical, safeDispatch refused all 11 submit-like fixture targets, overlay survives re-renders and body wipes, reload re-injection and idle-stop lazy reconnect work, registerContentScripts injects only once the host is granted.","files":null}]}